        "narration": "Maya plays ring toss at the fair. She scores 345 points. Her brother Sam scores 354 points. Who scored more?",
        "text": "345 or 354?",
        "visual": { "kind": "emoji", "emoji": "🎯", "count": null, "filled": null }
      },
      {
        "narration": "Start with the hundreds. Both numbers have 3 hundreds. That is a tie, so we look at the tens next.",
        "text": "3 hundreds and 3 hundreds",
        "visual": null
      },
      {
        "narration": "345 has 4 tens. 354 has 5 tens. 5 tens is more than 4 tens. So 354 is greater than 345.",
        "text": "354 is greater than 345",
        "visual": null
      },
      {
        "narration": "Later, Maya scores 620 and Sam scores 280. We can use 500 as a helper. 620 is more than 500. 280 is less than 500.",
        "text": "620 is greater than 500. 280 is less than 500.",
        "visual": null
      },
      {
        "narration": "So 620 is greater than 280. A helper number like 500 is a quick way to compare big gaps.",
        "text": "620 is greater than 280",
        "visual": null
      },
      {
        "narration": "To put numbers in order, find the least first. For 620, 280, and 345, the order from least to greatest is 280, 345, 620.",
        "text": "280, 345, 620",
        "visual": null
      },
      {
        "narration": "Greatest to least goes the other way. It is 620, 345, 280. Now let's practise comparing and ordering.",
        "text": "620, 345, 280",
        "visual": null
      }
    ],
